who would never stay out without letting someone in her family know first. They urged the police to question Danilo Restivo, but their request was dismissed, with the officers suggesting the claps return home and wait for Elisa to show up instead. Unsure of what else to do, Gildor returned to the church of the Holy Trinity, this time finding the door was locked. He tracked someone down who had access to the key and they led him inside to search the area once again. Gildor scoured the empty pews and as he approached the altar, noticed the wooden door that gave access to the upper levels of the church was locked. Gildor asked to gain entry, but was informed that the only person who had a key to the door was

